BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:planetenuhr-en-meteor-2026-01-04-quadrantids-meteor-shower-maximum@marsrakete.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260805T224557Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260105
SUMMARY:Quadrantids meteor shower maximum
CATEGORIES:METEOR
DESCRIPTION:Sichtbarkeit: Good from Europe before dawn\, but moonlight may interfere\n\nShort\, sharp maximum\; northern radiant is favorable for Europe.
X-PLANETENUHR-VISIBILITY:Good from Europe before dawn\, but moonlight may interfere
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:planetenuhr-en-meteor-2026-04-22-lyrids-meteor-shower-maximum@marsrakete.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260805T224557Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260422
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260423
SUMMARY:Lyrids meteor shower maximum
CATEGORIES:METEOR
DESCRIPTION:Sichtbarkeit: Visible from Europe after midnight\n\nModerate spring shower\; best from a dark site.
X-PLANETENUHR-VISIBILITY:Visible from Europe after midnight
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:planetenuhr-en-meteor-2026-05-06-eta-aquariids-meteor-shower-maximum@marsrakete.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260805T224557Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260506
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260507
SUMMARY:Eta Aquariids meteor shower maximum
CATEGORIES:METEOR
DESCRIPTION:Sichtbarkeit: Low radiant from Europe before dawn\n\nHalley-comet meteors\; better from southerly latitudes\, but some meteors are possible in Europe.
X-PLANETENUHR-VISIBILITY:Low radiant from Europe before dawn
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:planetenuhr-en-meteor-2026-07-30-delta-aquariids-meteor-shower-maximum@marsrakete.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260805T224557Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260731
SUMMARY:Delta Aquariids meteor shower maximum
CATEGORIES:METEOR
DESCRIPTION:Sichtbarkeit: Low southern radiant\; best from Europe after midnight\n\nPeak of a shower active roughly from 2026-07-12 to 2026-08-23\; darker skies away from city light help most.
X-PLANETENUHR-VISIBILITY:Low southern radiant\; best from Europe after midnight
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:planetenuhr-en-meteor-2026-07-31-alpha-capricornids-meteor-shower-maximum@marsrakete.github.io
